four-axis-ai-security-eval
==========================

four-axis-ai-security-eval is a four-axis LLM safety evaluation demo (15 benchmarks,
Streamlit UI). Evaluation engine files under
CybersecurityBenchmarks/benchmark/ originate from Meta's Purple Llama /
CyberSecEval (MIT License). The demo UI, judge postprocess, and the
five-prompt dataset subsets are included in this distribution.

Upstream dataset attribution (demo prompts are 5-item subsets):
- HarmBench — Center for AI Safety (2024)
- Misuse, Jailbreak, Exaggerated Safety — TrustLLM (2024) / XSTest
- Prompt Injection, Code Interpreter, MITRE ATT&CK, Vulnerability
  Exploitation, FRR — Purple Llama CyberSecEval
- AdvBench (2023)
- CySecBench (2025)
- RedCode (NeurIPS 2024)
- FalseReject — Amazon Science (2025)
- MMLU — Hendrycks et al. (2021)
- BIG-bench Hard — Suzgun et al. (2022)

Redistribute the demo JSON files only if each source license permits it.
The evaluation code does not grant additional rights to those datasets.

This demo includes prompts designed to elicit harmful or disallowed
model behavior. Use it only for research, evaluation, and defensive
alignment work. Do not use outputs to cause harm.
